        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "In a glovebox under rigorous exclusion of air and water, NaOCMe3 (277 mg, 2.88 mmol) was dissolved in 6 mL of THF and added by pipet to a stirred suspension of YCl3 (188 mg, 0.96 mmol) in 8 mL of THF. After stirring overnight, the mixture was centrifuged and the solution was decanted from a pasty insoluble residue (analyzed as 5% yttrium and discarded). Rotary evaporation of the solvent left colorless hexane-soluble 1 (268 mg, 80%). X-ray quality crystals were grown from concentrated toluene at 29 °C.",
