        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "In a glovebox, NaOCMe3 (294 mg, 3.06 mmol) was dissolved in 10 mL of THF and added by pipet to a stirred suspension of LaCl3 (250 mg, 1.02 mmol). After stirring 3 days, the mixture was centrifuged and the solution decanted from a pasty residue (6% La, discarded). Rotary evaporation left colorless 4 (361 mg, 87%). X-ray quality crystals were grown from concentrated toluene at −20 °C. Spectroscopic and analytical data were interpreted as the Cl-free analogue of 1/2 with both μ3 sites occupied by OCMe3; the associated CCDC deposition for this DOI is C40H88ClLa3O10 (GAGCEW).",
